    "b-index-dispatch-cycle-and-r-1": {
      "id": "b-index-dispatch-cycle-and-r-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Dispatch, Cycle, and Replay Events"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-dispatch-and-cycle-eve-2": {
      "id": "b-index-dispatch-and-cycle-eve-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Dispatch and cycle events preserve the accepted boundaries around workflow authority, handoff evidence, cycle closure, and recoverable evidence delivery. Their ordering and replay identities prevent retries from manufacturing a second accepted fact. See the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "event handshake",
          "attributes": {
            "link": "../../60-event-handshake"
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for scheduler wake-queue semantics and transactional framing."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-dispatch-handoff-3": {
      "id": "b-index-dispatch-handoff-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Dispatch handoff"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-an-occupied-lease-follow-4": {
      "id": "b-index-an-occupied-lease-follow-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "An occupied lease follows this accepted event order:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-text-5": {
      "id": "b-index-text-5",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "text"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "game.dispatch_requested\n  -> game.dispatch_drain_started\n  -> game.dispatch_released\n  -> game.dispatch_acquired"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-when-the-lease-is-free-6": {
      "id": "b-index-when-the-lease-is-free-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "When the lease is free, acquisition follows the request without drain or release. A blocker discovered during handoff produces "
        },
        {
          "insert": "game.dispatch_blocked",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and acquisition waits. A queued request may be cleared by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "game.dispatch_request_cancelled",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " without pretending that authority transferred."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-release-creates-one-immu-7": {
      "id": "b-index-release-creates-one-immu-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Release creates one immutable handoff snapshot. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "game.dispatch_released",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " carries its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "handoff_snapshot_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "handoff_snapshot_content_hash",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "; the successor "
        },
        {
          "insert": "game.dispatch_acquired",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " carries the same pair plus the new lease and accepted state revision. The snapshot persists the release event identity and zero or one acquisition identity. Consumers join the pair by snapshot identity and hash, not by timestamps, correlation, or trace."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-the-release-stays-in-the-8": {
      "id": "b-index-the-release-stays-in-the-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The release stays in the outgoing workflow's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "correlation_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "trace_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Acquisition and ingestion stay in the successor workflow's original correlation and trace. Their causation remains "
        },
        {
          "insert": "game.dispatch_released",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " to "
        },
        {
          "insert": "game.dispatch_acquired",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " to "
        },
        {
          "insert": "sync.ingesting",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", so the release-to-acquire link is the durable bridge across workflow-local lineage. Stable snapshot content yields a stable hash and snapshot identity; snapshot, release, and acquisition writes roll back together on failure."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-a-delayed-babysit-or-pro-9": {
      "id": "b-index-a-delayed-babysit-or-pro-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A delayed babysit or process-exit handoff is two accepted actions. Guardian settlement emits "
        },
        {
          "insert": "game.dispatch_released",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "run.paused",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " under the settlement command and settlement root span. The successor action emits "
        },
        {
          "insert": "game.dispatch_acquired",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "sync.ingesting",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " under the original queued operator "
        },
        {
          "insert": "sync.start",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " command and root span, with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "operator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " as actor. Immediate "
        },
        {
          "insert": "sync.start",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " uses the same operator provenance. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "sync.ingesting",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " accepts only "
        },
        {
          "insert": "operator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "runner",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", never "
        },
        {
          "insert": "guardian",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-transport-replay-10": {
      "id": "b-index-transport-replay-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Transport replay"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-each-accepted-game-ev-11": {
      "id": "b-index-each-accepted-game-ev-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Each accepted game-event transaction creates its outgoing spool deliveries in the same commit. A delivery identity is deterministic from "
        },
        {
          "insert": "event_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and destination. Delivery is at least once: a crash before acknowledgement redelivers the same identity, the consumer commits the identity with its effect, and a duplicate is an acknowledged no-op. A spool entry clears only after durable acceptance, and replay never appends another game event or reapplies an accepted fact."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-save-point-failure-repla-12": {
      "id": "b-index-save-point-failure-repla-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Save-point failure replay"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-a-failed-save-point-reco-13": {
      "id": "b-index-a-failed-save-point-reco-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A failed save point records "
        },
        {
          "insert": "cycle.save_point_failed",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", raises the matching blocker and stale flag, and uses a deterministic "
        },
        {
          "insert": "replay_key",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " derived from cycle, anchored commit, and trigger. If game storage was unavailable, the failure spool retains command, correlation, actor, span, and diagnostics; the next successful open replays the closed event payload transactionally. Concurrent or repeated opens deduplicate the same replay identity."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-a-successful-retry-write-14": {
      "id": "b-index-a-successful-retry-write-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A successful retry writes "
        },
        {
          "insert": "cycle.save_point_recorded",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " against the original anchor and includes "
        },
        {
          "insert": "replayed_failure_event_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " when applicable. The artifact set and timeline entry are written at most once. The matching blocker and stale flag clear only after the evidence is durable."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-the-entire-failure-spool-15": {
      "id": "b-index-the-entire-failure-spool-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The entire failure spool validates before replay begins. A malformed final "
        },
        {
          "insert": "*.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " spool file or invalid spool schema fails loudly with an error naming the path; the corrupt file is retained and no partial event is emitted. A missing spool directory is an empty spool."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-cycle-lifecycle-16": {
      "id": "b-index-cycle-lifecycle-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Cycle lifecycle"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-cycle-closing-is-the-17": {
      "id": "b-index-cycle-closing-is-the-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "cycle.closing",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the status-transition fact accepted when an operator starts a permitted close. A close blocked by lease ownership, unshipped work, stale evidence, dirty worktree evidence, or failed capture does not emit "
        },
        {
          "insert": "cycle.closed",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Entry into blocked status emits "
        },
        {
          "insert": "cycle.blocked",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " once with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prior_status = from_status",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", complete blocker/source/recovery facts, and the accepted state revision."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-index-while-a-cycle-remains-18": {
      "id": "b-index-while-a-cycle-remains-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "While a cycle remains blocked, membership changes emit "
        },
        {
          "insert": "cycle.blockers_updated",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with added, removed, and complete current blocker-code sets; the event is progress, not another blocked-status entry. After the close gates and final save point succeed, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "cycle.closed",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " records the final head, shipped and unshipped work summary, final save-point identity, closing operator, and state revision. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "cycle.complete",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the separate status-transition fact for entering the complete cycle phase."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
}
